message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "QH2DC: Grid-Connection-Aware Scheduling of AI Data Centres with Green Hydrogen and Quantum-Assisted Workload Placement"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Manjunath"
    given-names: "Pavan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2694-8807"
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pavangemmanjunath-cell/Grid-Aware-AI-Datacenter-Scheduling"
url: "https://github.com/pavangemmanjunath-cell/Grid-Aware-AI-Datacenter-Scheduling"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  Research software for minimising the grid connection capacity an AI
  data-centre campus requires. A mixed-integer scheduler co-dispatches grid
  import, an electrolyser, a hydrogen tank and a fuel cell together with the
  placement of delay-tolerant AI workload bundles, under firm, phased and
  non-firm (time-varying) connection envelopes; the smallest feasible uniform
  capacity is found by bisection. The daily placement sub-problem is also
  written as a 12-variable QUBO and solved with an exact state-vector QAOA,
  verified against exhaustive enumeration. The repository contains the MATLAB
  reference implementation, an independent Python/SciPy cross-check, a FastAPI
  simulation service with a React/three.js web simulator, and a deterministic
  synthetic 168-hour benchmark. No quantum advantage is claimed.
keywords:
  - AI data centre
  - grid connection capacity
  - non-firm connection
  - green hydrogen
  - workload flexibility
  - mixed-integer linear programming
  - QUBO
  - QAOA
  - energy systems optimisation
  - reproducible research
